# Entirely fictional university enquiries; no real student records or identifiers.
# Route the main request, not the student's eligibility, health or academic ability.
# One item per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
What are the entry requirements for the undergraduate engineering programme?
I have an offer to start in September. Can I defer my place until next year?
Which supporting documents do I need to submit with my postgraduate application?
I am studying elsewhere and would like to transfer into your history degree. How do I apply?
Can I pay my tuition fees in instalments rather than all at once?
Where can I find scholarships for the master's programme?
My student loan is delayed. Is there a hardship fund I can apply to for help with living costs?
My tuition invoice shows the wrong amount. Who can review the charge?
When do applications for a room in university halls open?
My room allocation is much farther from campus than I expected. Can I request a room change?
The radiator in my university residence is not working. How do I report a repair?
My accommodation contract ends before my last exam. Can I extend my stay in halls?
Two of my compulsory lectures appear at the same time. Can someone resolve the timetable clash?
Where will next week's chemistry lab take place, and what time does it start?
Can I move to a different seminar group because it clashes with another class?
My exam timetable lists two different rooms for the same paper. Which room should I attend?
I cannot sign in to the admissions portal because the password reset link never arrives.
The campus Wi-Fi connects on my laptop but will not let me access any websites.
I changed my phone and can no longer approve MFA requests for my university email.
The online timetable page gives an error whenever I open it, even after trying another browser.
I have been feeling overwhelmed by the move to university. How can I arrange a wellbeing appointment?
Where can I find information about the university's confidential counselling service?
I am finding it difficult to settle in and would like to speak to someone about feeling lonely.
Exams are making me anxious. Does the student wellbeing team offer workshops on managing stress?
How do I renew a library book that is due back tomorrow?
Where can I find a list of student societies and how to join them?
Can the careers service help me prepare for an internship interview?
I need some help with university life but am not sure what information to provide.
